							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=823.msg7982#msg7982">Quote from: EQSysquella on May 18, 2004, 01:41:02 am</a></div><div class="quote">Well teachers were showing this to there students (High School), which they are getting reamed for &gt;&lt;<br /></div><br />Rightfully so. Those kind of graphic images have no educational value, they provide a soapbox for the teacher. Even if the subject is of value in a classroom, (which I feel it is) to show the images to a class of high school students is inappropriate.<br /><br />Sure the students can access the internet and find them eventually on their own, but that does not justify a teacher forcing those images on the students. If the teachers are getting reamed for it, kudos to the administrators.<br /><br />I am all about &quot;freedom of speech&quot; but a teacher holds a position of abnormal influence and control over students in a classroom, and I don&#039;t think that power should be abused. <br />
						</td>
